{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Circumcise the foreskin of your heart</b> — that your heart be open to knowing the truth, not as you have done until this day, for HaShem did not give you a heart to know, eyes to see, and ears to hear." "<b>And stiffen your neck no more</b> — that you not be like your fathers, a stubborn and rebellious generation, who dwelt among the Egyptians and learned their deeds, and were hard in abandoning their ways, as they did in making the calf, and there He called them (Exodus 32:9) \"a stiff-necked people,\" for they would not turn back from the error that had entered their hearts, thinking that there is benefit in the worship of the angels or the host of heaven. But you shall know and understand and believe that HaShem your Elohim, He is Elohim of the elohim and Adonai of the lords — Elohim of the elohim means the angels on high, and Adonai of the lords means all the host of heaven who have dominion over the lower realms, for He is the Master who established their governance on earth, and His is the greatness and the might, and He is awesome in the splendor of His strength, who does not show favoritism to any one of the elohim or the lords to defend their worshippers, and does not take a bribe from a person's hand. And they explained the bribe as follows: even a perfect saint who commits a transgression — He does not accept from him the performance of a commandment among His commandments as a bribe to atone for him, but rather punishes him for his sins and rewards him for all his good deeds. And Onkelos translated: \"who before Him there is no taking of favor, and who does not accept a bribe\" — his intent is to explain that this is among the attributes of negation in the Creator, blessed be He; Scripture says that there is no such thing as the Name showing favoritism, for man, living being, does not see Him, and all is as nothing before Him, and from emptiness and void they are reckoned to Him; and there is no such thing as His taking a bribe and money from a person as kings and judges of the earth do. And the correct interpretation in my eyes is: \"who does not show favoritism\" — to the great ones of mankind in their dispute with their inferiors; \"and does not take a bribe\" — from their rich ones in their dispute with the poor, for He executes justice for the orphan and the widow against the great ones, and establishes their fixed portion of life. \"And loves the ger, to give him bread and clothing\" — and these are all human needs, and behold He provides for the poor who have no friend or companion."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {1 "In the phrase וקבע את קבעיהם נפש, I read קבע as 'fixed portion/sustenance'; the expression is unusual and may reflect a textual variant."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:47:46.587981751Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}